<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Drug-susceptible pulmonary tuberculosis, continuation phase (A15.0)</content>. Intensive phase complete with full adherence and a good clinical response. Liver tests normal (ALT 38, AST 35, bilirubin 0.7). Because the disease was cavitary, the two-month culture taken today decides the length of the continuation phase: four months if negative, seven if positive. Dr. Navarro reviewed the plan by message today and agreed. [S]<list><item>Continue isoniazid 300 mg, rifampin 600 mg, and pyridoxine daily by video.</item><item>Sputum smear and culture today (induced, because he no longer coughs up sputum).</item><item>Monthly liver tests and symptom review continue.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alcohol use disorder, mild (F10.10)</content>. No alcohol for seven weeks. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide. [S]<list><item>Continue counseling every two weeks.</item><item>Plan ahead for social events where he used to drink.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Symptom review: cough, sputum, hemoptysis, fever, night sweats</td><td>At least monthly during treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight</td><td>At least monthly during treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>62.5 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Hepatitis symptom review (nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, jaundice, dark urine)</td><td>Every visit and every observed dose</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Liver tests (ALT, AST, bilirubin)</td><td>Baseline, at two weeks, then monthly because of alcohol use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>ALT 38, AST 35 U/L, bilirubin 0.7 mg/dL, all normal</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Two-month sputum culture</td><td>At the end of the intensive phase; decides the continuation length in cavitary disease</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Induced sputum smear negative today; culture sent, final reading in six weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Sputum AFB smear and culture</td><td>Monthly until two consecutive cultures are negative</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Third-week cultures show no growth so far; final next week</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Chest X-ray</td><td>At diagnosis; at two months only if the first cultures were negative; at the end of treatment as a new baseline</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not needed at two months, because the first cultures were positive</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Doses observed and missed (video-observed therapy)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>All 56 intensive-phase doses observed</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Peripheral neuropathy check, with pyridoxine</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No neuropathy</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Contact investigation (household, coworkers, patients)</td><td>Led by the health department, from diagnosis</td><td>Referred</td><td>Health department continuing; no results are part of his record</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Alcohol use (AUDIT-C for the past month)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 1 for the past month</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Brief counseling about alcohol and liver risk</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Social events planned for</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Counseling with a substance-use counselor</td><td>Every one to two weeks during treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Every two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide-risk review and safety plan, with the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No thoughts of suicide</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Infectious diseases review</td><td>At two months and at the end of treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dr. Navarro reviewed the plan by message today</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Complete 182 doses of treatment under video-observed therapy within six months. In progress; target 2026-08-18 [S]</item><item>Sputum culture negative at two months. In progress; target 2026-08-18 [S]</item><item>No alcohol during treatment, to protect his liver. In progress; target 2026-08-18 [S]</item><item>Return to work once he is no longer infectious. Outcome by 2026-03-17: Released from home isolation after three negative sputum smears and back at work four weeks into treatment [S]</item><item>Weight back to at least 64 kg by the end of treatment. In progress; target 2026-08-18 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Official American Thoracic Society/Centers for Disease Control and Prevention/Infectious Diseases Society of America Clinical Practice Guidelines: Treatment of Drug-Susceptible Tuberculosis (2016); An official ATS statement: hepatotoxicity of antituberculosis therapy (2006); Guidelines for the investigation of contacts of persons with infectious tuberculosis: recommendations from the National Tuberculosis Controllers Association and CDC (2005); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Substance Use Disorders (2021); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: End-of-treatment visit after the last dose. Monthly liver tests and symptom review in between. Call the same day for hepatitis symptoms or a returning cough. Next scheduled visit 2026-08-18: end-of-treatment review after six months. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
